---
import MainLayout from "../../layouts/MainLayout.astro";
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import img1 from "../../images/comics/Cover.png";
import img2 from "../../images/comics/ComicPage1.png";
import img3 from "../../images/comics/ComicPage2.png";
import img4 from "../../images/comics/ComicPage3.png";
import img5 from "../../images/comics/ComicPage4.png";
import img6 from "../../images/comics/pearl-wip1.jpg";
import img9 from "../../images/comics/Back 2.png";
import img10 from "../../images/comics/Ideation.jpg";
import img11 from "../../images/comics/Ideation 2.jpg";
import img12 from "../../images/comics/Ideation 3.jpg";

const pages = [
  { src: img1, alt: "Pearl Page 1" },
  { src: img2, alt: "Pearl Page 2" },
  { src: img3, alt: "Pearl Page 3" },
  { src: img4, alt: "Pearl Page 4" },
  { src: img5, alt: "Pearl Page 5" },
  { src: img9, alt: "Pearl Back Cover" }
];
const wippages = [
  { src: img12, alt: "Pearl WIP 4" },
  { src: img10, alt: "Pearl WIP 2" },
  { src: img11, alt: "Pearl WIP 3" },
  { src: img6, alt: "Pearl WIP 1" }
];
---
<MainLayout title="Pearl | Comic">
    <section class="container">
        <h1 class="title heading">Pearl</h1>
        <div class="image-list">
            {pages.map((page) => (
                <Image src={page.src} alt={page.alt} />
            ))}
        </div>
        <h3>Ink on paper, Digital</h3>
        <p>
            This is a four-page comic I created as a part of the Illustration and Visual Storytelling residency at the School of Visual Arts.
        </p>
        <p>
            Inspired by nightmares I would have from being chased by a demon.
        I think that dreams reflect our mental state – I often run away from
        my problems and it comes out through my dreams.
        I created a story where a character would ultimately be forced to
        make a choice and either be brave and face her demon, or keep
        running away and potentially lose it all in the process.
        The inspiration for the characters came from me being curious
        about my birth stone, the pearl. I found out that vinegar can
        dissolve genuine pearls and thought this would be an interesting
        dynamic for opposing characters.
        </p>
        <div class="image-list">
            {wippages.map((page) => (
                <Image src={page.src} alt={page.alt} />
            ))}
        </div>
        <h3>Process</h3>
        <p>The requirements for this project was to create a four-page comic on anything we chose. To start, I brainstormed story ideas until I landed on this one. Then, I freely doodled the start, middle, and end of the story. From there, I dove into character design and then thumbnailing each page. We met with a comics professor once a week over about 4 weeks and had each step in the comics process reviewed 1-on-1. </p>
            <p>I challenged myself to start drawing the comic traditionally, with a comic art board for the very first time. It was new to me and a lot of fun. I also noticed how different the strokes turn out traditionally versus digitally -- they look much more organic with a brush pen.
                Additionally, I wanted to make it into an actual comic format with a cover and inside covers, so I designed a cover page and inside pages to make small zines of them to distribute.
            </p>
            <p>In hindsight, it was difficult to condense my story into just four pages, but I learned a lot from the process, and would probably aim to let the pages and story breathe a little more within the restraints.</p>
    </section>
</MainLayout>
<style>
.container {
    justify-content: center;
    padding: 2rem;
    text-align: left;
}
img {
    max-width: 500px;
    max-height: 300px;
    width: auto;
    height: auto;
}
.image-list {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    grid-gap: 1rem;
    justify-content: left;
}
</style>